  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m meticulously dissecting the user\'s explicit specifications, starting with the application\'s name: \"Smart Attendance System.\" I am cross-referencing this against the required skills and best practices. My plan is to ensure that I address the explicit and implicit requirements of this.\n\n\n**Implementing Firebase & Design**\n\nI\'ve just finished setting up the Firebase configuration using the provided details for `attendence-92251`, ensuring I export `auth` and `db` from `src/firebase.ts`. I\'m employing the modular Firebase v9+ SDK for this. I\'ve also implemented the helper function to manage account creation without requiring a full sign-out. The design phase has begun, focusing on a calm and minimalist aesthetic with ample white space. I\'m leaning towards a soft off-white background in light mode and a deep obsidian/zinc tone in dark mode, accented with a warm amber color for visual appeal.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the specific user interface elements. I\'ve specified font loading for \"Inter\", \"Noto Sans Devanagari\", and \"JetBrains Mono\" as requested. I\'ve also detailed the dark mode toggle implementation and the use of zero-pill design for static metadata and clean, interactive tabs. The top bar on the landing page is planned with a sticky design, incorporating a logo, links, language toggle, dark mode toggle, and a \"Start Free\" button with a hamburger menu for smaller screens. The language toggle is being built to sit both in the landing page top bar, and inside the app header. I will store the user\'s language preference in `localStorage`\n\n\n**Defining Locale and Packages**\n\nI\'m now determining locale-specific formats for dates and numbers using `Intl.DateTimeFormat` and `Intl.NumberFormat`, targeting `en-IN` and `hi-IN`. I\'ve also identified natural Hindi translations for key terms like \"Mark Attendance\" (\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\234\340\244\274\340\244\277\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\262\340\244\227\340\244\276\340\244\217\340\244\201). Furthermore, I\'ve listed the tech stack packages and will execute a batched installation. Finally, I\'m setting up PWA using `vite-plugin-pwa`.\n\n\n**Finalizing PWA Setup**\n\nI\'ve just added the PWA configuration details, including setting `type: \'module\'`, the manifest with the specified properties, and ensuring valid PNG icon files are created, which I will accomplish by a node script. Furthermore, I\'ll add `\"vite-plugin-pwa/client\"` to `tsconfig.json`, followed by the implementation of `usePWAInstall`, `PWAInstallButton`, and `OfflineIndicator`.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now detailing the database schema with Firebase, outlining the structures for users, attendance records, leaves, announcements, notifications, and messages. I am defining fields like `uid`, `name`, `email`, `role`, and timestamps for each collection, ensuring consistency and data integrity, in the context of the requested app.\n\n\n**Mapping Route Definitions**\n\nI\'m now detailing all required application routes. I have identified the following: `/`, `/login`, `/register`, `/forgot-password`, and `/pending`. I am also planning the dashboard implementation for Admin, Manager and Member roles, with dedicated pages for Managers, and Members within their section. I will be using either a role-aware router or separate routes to handle this. Finally, the Mark Attendance section has been designed, which will be accessible by scanning.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Implementations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of key features. I\'m focusing on the QR tab, detailing the integration of `html5-qrcode` with front/back camera switching, and continuous scanning with a 2-second cooldown, complete with Web Audio API beep and vibration on scan. I\'m implementing UI elements for scanned data and handling late detection. I\'m also planning the Manual tab with search, and present/absent/leave options, alongside bulk modes.\nI\'m now planning the implementation for the `/leaves`, `/announcements`, and `/reports` routes. I am also planning the design for the leave requests workflow, and announcement posting and display.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing the member dashboard and admin/settings sections. I\'m planning the `/member` dashboard to include a QR code, member ID, monthly calendar, and attendance history. Also, I\'m working on the `/settings` routes, planning features such as personal profiles, organization settings, language selection, dark mode toggle, and PWA install. For the reports, I will include features for a date range, person, status, tables, charts, and exports.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Nf_-av2fIZ_oz7IPuNuHqQ4"
