    thinking: "**Defining Core Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m building out the clean folder structure and core architecture now. I\'ve got `src/firebase.ts` sketched out. It\'ll house the exact user-provided Firebase config and export `auth`, `db`, and a helpful `createSecondaryAccount` function leveraging a secondary Firebase app. The function will utilize `initializeApp` with a \'secondary\' app name.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Flows**\n\nI\'ve been working on authentication flows, specifically `createUserWithEmailAndPassword`, `sendPasswordResetEmail`, and `signOut` functionality for a secondary auth instance. The TypeScript interfaces are defined in `src/types/index.ts`, covering all relevant data structures. Translations for English and Hindi are completed in `src/i18n`, including every screen element. The Language context manages locale, while theme context has Light/Dark toggle.\n\n\n**Refining Contextual States**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `AuthContext` to manage authentication state, user profiles, and organization data with Firebase subscriptions. I\'ve integrated `onAuthStateChanged` and set up real-time updates for user and organization details. Also, I\'ve exposed methods for logout, refreshing org data, and a role label helper.\n\n**Developing Core Data Services**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the data services. I\'m building out atomic counters for organization management (`ORG-MGR-0001`, `ORG-MEM-0001`). Also, I\'m working on manager codes. I\'m implementing bulk CSV user addition, self-registration with pending status, and approval/rejection workflows, including atomic ID assignment. I\'m refining user management functionality, including editing, activating/deactivating, and deleting user records.\nI have also begun building the `attendanceService.ts` module.\n\n\n**Constructing Component Library**\n\nI\'m now building out the component library. I have the beginnings of the UI components: `Logo`, `LanguageToggle`, `ThemeToggle`, `PWAInstallButton`, `OfflineIndicator`, `Layout`, and `QRCardModal`. Also, I\'m working on hooks, specifically `useTranslation`, `usePWAInstall`, and `useOnlineStatus`. Furthermore, I\'ve got the `demoService.ts` module with functions to load and delete demo data.\n\n\n**Defining Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on page structure, creating the foundational files and components in parallel. Specifically, I\'m defining the `ProtectedRoute`, skeleton and empty state components, along with all the core page modules in `src/pages`. The landing and authentication pages are ready. I\'m also preparing `firestore.rules`, `firestore.indexes.json`, and `README.md`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "jP_-au61BOafz7IPz52MsAo"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_17581814723741134395"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { initializeApp, getApps, getApp } from \'firebase/app\';\\nimport {\\n  getAuth,\\n  createUserWithEmailAndPassword,\\n  sendPasswordResetEmail,\\n  signOut,\\n} from \'firebase/auth\';\\nimport { getFirestore } from \'firebase/firestore\';\\n\\nexport const firebaseConfig = {\\n  apiKey: \\\"AIzaSyB4O0_f2y6D3No4kKw3PALtfO_6v2s6lAQ\\\",\\n  authDomain: \\\"attendence-92251.firebaseapp.com\\\",\\n  projectId: \\\"attendence-92251\\\",\\n  storageBucket: \\\"attendence-92251.firebasestorage.app\\\",\\n  messagingSenderId: \\\"327288246371\\\",\\n  appId: \\\"1:327288246371:web:bf97d084314aa9ea726856\\\",\\n  measurementId: \\\"G-FQP60QRQRP\\\"\\n};\\n\\nconst app = getApps().some((a) => a.name === \'[DEFAULT]\')\\n  ? getApp()\\n  : initializeApp(firebaseConfig);\\n\\nexport const auth = getAuth(app);\\nexport const db = getFirestore(app);\\n\\nfunction getSecondaryAuth() {\\n  const existing = getApps().find((a) => a.name === \'secondary\');\\n  const secondaryApp = existing ?? initializeApp(firebaseConfig, \'secondary\');\\n  return getAuth(secondaryApp);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Creates a Firebase Auth account using a secondary Firebase App instance\\n * so the currently logged-in Admin or Manager is NOT signed out.\\n * Also sends a password-reset email so the new person can set their own password.\\n */\\nexport async function createSecondaryAccount(\\n  email: string,\\n  tempPassword?: string\\n): Promise<{ uid: string; resetEmailSent: boolean }> {\\n  const secondaryAuth = getSecondaryAuth();\\n  const generatedPassword =\\n    tempPassword ||\\n    `Tmp!${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10)}${Date.now().toString(36).slice(-4)}`;\\n\\n  try {\\n    const cred = await createUserWithEmailAndPassword(\\n      secondaryAuth,\\n      email.trim().toLowerCase(),\\n      generatedPassword\\n    );\\n    const uid = cred.user.uid;\\n\\n    let resetEmailSent = false;\\n    try {\\n      await sendPasswordResetEmail(secondaryAuth, email.trim().toLowerCase());\\n      resetEmailSent = true;\\n    } catch {\\n      // Non-fatal: account is created; admin can remind user to use Forgot Password\\n      resetEmailSent = false;\\n    }\\n\\n    await signOut(secondaryAuth);\\n    return { uid, resetEmailSent };\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    try {\\n      await signOut(secondaryAuth);\\n    } catch {\\n      // Ignore cleanup error\\n    }\\n    throw err;\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create src/firebase.ts with exact provided config, auth/db exports, and secondary app account creation helper\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/firebase.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating Firebase configuration\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create src/firebase.ts\"}"
