  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Service Layer**\n\nI\'m currently focused on parallelizing the service layer update, specifically `userService.ts`. The recent change involves replacing `allocateMemberId` with a new function, `allocateUniqueUserId`. This new function takes additional parameters and extracts a unique ID prefix from a name to streamline member identification. This should greatly speed up things, and enhance unique id creation.\n\n\n**Refining Unique ID Allocation**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on unique ID generation, particularly within `allocateUniqueUserId`. The system now leverages a Firestore transaction with up to 30 attempts, incorporating random 3-digit suffixes and letter rotations if collisions persist. I\'ve also integrated the new ID allocation into `addPersonDirect`, `selfRegisterUser`, `approvePendingUser`, and `deleteUserProfile`. Furthermore, I\'ve modified `createOrganizationAndAdmin` to assign a unique ID for the admin user. Finally, default organization settings and demo user updates are proceeding.\n\n\n**Implementing Demo Data**\n\nI\'m now generating realistic demo user IDs like `KAV482` with the `isDemo: true` flag, and also ensuring the `deleteDemoData` function cleans them up. Attendance data is being tagged with a mix of \'live_qr\', \'live_code\', and \'manual\' attendances.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Introducing Session Service**\n\nI\'ve also introduced a new `sessionService.ts`. I\'m working on the `startAttendanceSession` function, which creates session tokens and codes. It generates a 128-bit token, a 6-digit code, and calculates latitude cosine and `endsAt` timestamp. It creates entries in both `sessions/{sessionId}` and `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}`, and returns essential session details. The next step is the `rotateSessionSecret` function.\n\n\n**Expanding Session Features**\n\nI\'m now expanding the `sessionService`. The focus is now on several new functionalities. These include rotating session secrets, session extension and closure, and functions to locate active sessions for members and managers. I\'m also implementing the data subscription functions. Additional functions are being added to log failed attempts and submit self-attendance entries.\n\n\n**Consolidating Atomic Writes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on atomic operations. My current priority is to ensure that attendance data, specifically `attendance/{orgId}_{date}_{personUid}` and session device data (`sessionDevices/{sessionId}_{deviceId}`), is written in a single atomic `writeBatch`. I\'m also implementing the permission-denied diagnoses, logging attempts accordingly.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "ogz_auHHL6GVmtkP9ea3oAE"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8998832684038258254"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { createUserWithEmailAndPassword } from \'firebase/auth\';\\nimport {\\n  collection,\\n  deleteDoc,\\n  doc,\\n  getDoc,\\n  getDocs,\\n  query,\\n  runTransaction,\\n  serverTimestamp,\\n  setDoc,\\n  updateDoc,\\n  where,\\n} from \'firebase/firestore\';\\nimport { auth, createSecondaryAccount, db } from \'../firebase\';\\nimport type { LanguageCode, Organization, UserProfile, UserRole, UserStatus } from \'../types\';\\nimport {\\n  extractIdPrefixFromName,\\n  generateCandidateUserId,\\n  generateCode,\\n} from \'../utils/helpers\';\\nimport { createNotification } from \'./communicationService\';\\n\\nexport async function generateUniqueManagerCode(): Promise<string> {\\n  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 10; attempt++) {\\n    const code = generateCode(6);\\n    const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \'managerCodes\', code));\\n    if (!snap.exists()) return code;\\n  }\\n  return generateCode(8);\\n}\\n\\nconst ALPHABET = \'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\';\\n\\n/**\\n * Atomically reserves a globally unique 6-character ID (e.g. PAN482)\\n * using a Firestore transaction on the `userIds/{ID}` lookup collection.\\n * Retries up to 30 times with new random 3 digits; if exhausted, changes the 3rd letter.\\n */\\nexport async function allocateUniqueUserId(params: {\\n  nameForId: string;\\n  uid: string;\\n  orgId: string;\\n  role: UserRole;\\n  isDemo?: boolean;\\n}): Promise<string> {\\n  const basePrefix = extractIdPrefixFromName(params.nameForId);\\n  const firstTwo = basePrefix.slice(0, 2);\\n  const startThirdIdx = Math.max(0, ALPHABET.indexOf(basePrefix[2] || \'X\'));\\n\\n  for (let letterStep = 0; letterStep < 26; letterStep++) {\\n    const thirdChar = ALPHABET[(startThirdIdx + letterStep) % 26];\\n    const prefix = `${firstTwo}${thirdChar}`;\\n\\n    for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 30; attempt++) {\\n      const candidate = generateCandidateUserId(prefix);\\n      const idRef = doc(db, \'userIds\', candidate);\\n      try {\\n        const reserved = await runTransaction(db, async (tx) => {\\n          const snap = await tx.get(idRef);\\n          if (snap.exists()) return false;\\n          tx.set(idRef, {\\n            uid: params.uid,\\n            orgId: params.orgId,\\n            role: params.role,\\n            ...(params.isDemo ? { isDemo: true } : {}),\\n            createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n          });\\n          return true;\\n        });\\n        if (reserved) return candidate;\\n      } catch {\\n        // Collision or transaction retry contention \342\200\224 try next candidate\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  throw new Error(\'Could not allocate unique 6-character ID\');\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Directly adds a Manager (by Admin) or Member (by Manager/Admin).\\n * Uses the secondary Firebase Auth instance so the current user stays signed in.\\n */\\nexport async function addPersonDirect(params: {\\n  org: Organization;\\n  role: \'manager\' | \'member\';\\n  managerId: string | null;\\n  name: string;\\n  englishName?: string;\\n  email: string;\\n  phone: string;\\n  rollNumber?: string;\\n  language?: LanguageCode;\\n}): Promise<{ profile: UserProfile; resetEmailSent: boolean }> {\\n  const cleanEmail = params.email.trim().toLowerCase();\\n  const { uid, resetEmailSent } = await createSecondaryAccount(cleanEmail);\\n\\n  const memberId = await allocateUniqueUserId({\\n    nameForId: params.englishName?.trim() || params.name,\\n    uid,\\n    orgId: params.org.id,\\n    role: params.role,\\n  });\\n\\n  let managerCode: string | undefined;\\n  if (params.role === \'manager\') {\\n    managerCode = await generateUniqueManagerCode();\\n    await setDoc(doc(db, \'managerCodes\', managerCode), {\\n      orgId: params.org.id,\\n      managerUid: uid,\\n      managerName: params.name.trim(),\\n      orgName: params.org.name,\\n      roleLabels: params.org.roleLabels,\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  const userDoc: Omit<UserProfile, \'createdAt\'> & { createdAt: ReturnType<typeof serverTimestamp> } = {\\n    uid,\\n    name: params.name.trim(),\\n    ...(params.englishName?.trim() ? { englishName: params.englishName.trim() } : {}),\\n    email: cleanEmail,\\n    phone: params.phone.trim(),\\n    rollNumber: params.rollNumber?.trim() || \'\',\\n    role: params.role,\\n    orgId: params.org.id,\\n    managerId: params.role === \'member\' ? params.managerId : null,\\n    memberId,\\n    status: \'active\',\\n    ...(managerCode ? { managerCode } : {}),\\n    language: params.language || \'en\',\\n    createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n  };\\n\\n  await setDoc(doc(db, \'users\', uid), userDoc);\\n\\n  return {\\n    profile: { ...userDoc, createdAt: null } as UserProfile,\\n    resetEmailSent,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Self-registration for a Manager (using Organization Code) or Member (using Manager Code).\\n * Status starts as \'pending\' until approved by parent.\\n */\\nexport async function selfRegisterUser(params: {\\n  role: \'manager\' | \'member\';\\n  orgId: string;\\n  managerId: string | null;\\n  parentNotifyUid: string | null;\\n  name: string;\\n  englishName?: string;\\n  email: string;\\n  password: string;\\n  phone: string;\\n  rollNumber?: string;\\n  language: LanguageCode;\\n}): Promise<string> {\\n  const cleanEmail = params.email.trim().toLowerCase();\\n  const cred = await createUserWithEmailAndPassword(auth, cleanEmail, params.password);\\n  const uid = cred.user.uid;\\n\\n  await setDoc(doc(db, \'users\', uid), {\\n    uid,\\n    name: params.name.trim(),\\n    ...(params.englishName?.trim() ? { englishName: params.englishName.trim() } : {}),\\n    email: cleanEmail,\\n    phone: params.phone.trim(),\\n    rollNumber: params.rollNumber?.trim() || \'\',\\n    role: params.role,\\n    orgId: params.orgId,\\n    managerId: params.role === \'member\' ? params.managerId : null,\\n    memberId: \'\',\\n    status: \'pending\',\\n    language: params.language,\\n    createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\\n  });\\n\\n  if (params.parentNotifyUid) {\\n    try {\\n      await createNotification({\\n        orgId: params.orgId,\\n        toUid: params.parentNotifyUid,\\n        type: \'approval\',\\n        text: `${params.name.trim()} requested to join as ${params.role}.`,\\n      });\\n    } catch {\\n      // Non-fatal\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return uid;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function approvePendingUser(org: Organization, person: UserProfile): Promise<void> {\\n  if (person.role === \'admin\') return;\\n  const memberId =\\n    person.memberId ||\\n    (await allocateUniqueUserId({\\n      nameForId: person.englishName || person.name,\\n      uid: person.uid,\\n      orgId: org.id,\\n      role: person.role,\\n    }));\\n\\n  const patch: Record<string, unknown> = {\\n    status: \'active\',\\n    memberId,\\n  };\\n\\n  if (person.role === \'manager\' && !person.managerCode) {\\n    const code = await generateUniqueManagerCode();\\n    patch.managerCode = code;\\n    await setDoc(doc(db, \'managerCodes\', code), {\\n      orgId: org.id,\\n      managerUid: person.uid,\\n      managerName: person.name,\\n      orgName: org.name,\\n      roleLabels: org.roleLabels,\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  await updateDoc(doc(db, \'users\', person.uid), patch);\\n\\n  await createNotification({\\n    orgId: org.id,\\n    toUid: person.uid,\\n    type: \'approval\',\\n    text: `Your account has been approved. Your unique ID is ${memberId}.`,\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport async function rejectPendingUser(orgId: string, person: UserProfile): Promise<void> {\\n  await updateDoc(doc(db, \'users\', person.uid), { status: \'inactive\' });\\n  await createNotification({\\n    orgId,\\n    toUid: person.uid,\\n    type: \'approval\',\\n    text: \'Your registration request was not approved.\',\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport async function updateUserDetails(\\n  uid: string,\\n  updates: Partial<Pick<UserProfile, \'name\' | \'phone\' | \'rollNumber\' | \'language\'>>\\n): Promise<void> {\\n  await updateDoc(doc(db, \'users\', uid), updates as Record<string, unknown>);\\n}\\n\\nexport async function setUserStatus(uid: string, status: UserStatus): Promise<void> {\\n  await updateDoc(doc(db, \'users\', uid), { status });\\n}\\n\\nexport async function deleteUserProfile(person: UserProfile): Promise<void> {\\n  if (person.managerCode) {\\n    try {\\n      await deleteDoc(doc(db, \'managerCodes\', person.managerCode));\\n    } catch {\\n      // Ignore if already removed\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (person.memberId && /^[A-Z]{3}\\\\d{3}$/.test(person.memberId)) {\\n    try {\\n      await deleteDoc(doc(db, \'userIds\', person.memberId));\\n    } catch {\\n      // Ignore if already removed\\n    }\\n  }\\n  await deleteDoc(doc(db, \'users\', person.uid));\\n}\\n\\nexport async function fetchOrgUsers(\\n  orgId: string,\\n  role?: \'manager\' | \'member\'\\n): Promise<UserProfile[]> {\\n  const constraints = [where(\'orgId\', \'==\', orgId)];\\n  if (role) constraints.push(where(\'role\', \'==\', role));\\n  const q = query(collection(db, \'users\'), ...constraints);\\n  const snap = await getDocs(q);\\n  return snap.docs\\n    .map((d) => ({ ...(d.data() as UserProfile), uid: d.id }))\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\\n}\\n\\nexport async function fetchManagerMembers(\\n  orgId: string,\\n  managerUid: string\\n): Promise<UserProfile[]> {\\n  const q = query(\\n    collection(db, \'users\'),\\n    where(\'orgId\', \'==\', orgId),\\n    where(\'managerId\', \'==\', managerUid)\\n  );\\n  const snap = await getDocs(q);\\n  return snap.docs\\n    .map((d) => ({ ...(d.data() as UserProfile), uid: d.id }))\\n    .filter((u) => u.role === \'member\')\\n    .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Replace ORG-MEM-0001 counter with globally unique 6-character IDs reserved via Firestore transaction in userIds/{ID}\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/services/userService.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating userService for 6-char IDs\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update src/services/userService.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\362)\n\357)\001i\024}\023\210/\364\006\274\216(\217.T]\357\202o\020.Dla2\t\022)\2565\334\330\200\230\335\376\340\004\027\017*\330\262qaldE\313\315\235\225\314\261\340#\224\316O\237N\031\232\3053\340\304T\330\270\343!T\036\264o\023\263\213\305\350\276\2653\322{\276\203\313\351F$\301\\\365\354\330\322\332\252\034\353\037\345\002>\367\250{\373\314b\227@\243.\364\321m\3634L\242\005\305\322\346\037\222\016\245\262=\276Mn\332P\"a\215\307x\215]\034\210\n\265*E\357j4\222\257\246*)\236p34\226\356D\301p\222\371%\374\177\373o\003\361\335Zx\240\251\363S\000\326\024\252\270\001&\266\037$[\000\310\262\375\372\240\376\r\020\205\\2\235\302Q\326\242w\263Y\003%\347MmxKklvm\362\316\300r>\235\222\260\177\346\337\350p\204|\361\226,#\003`\243c+p=;wN\343F\344E\365\317\2219\245\032m\032O4\246\006\211\303\001\0015\337\341m\250\006\322R2D\277\372\325F{J\004\230\277\rK\203\251\276\373\300\340\021&\314P\365K$W\303\253\346\0034\234\360\246\210\353\323\"H=F\215\371\360o\001;\260B^\263F\017\370\264B\247\264q\301\026\241\264K\333\324\254O\374s\3354J\360`\b\205\025S\207=9\300s\363\3166@#\002$b\304\313F\343@8\243\205\024\267\322p*\303\235K\332\017\231.\231\301l\312g\362\374\324[\034\364\303sTy\225uc\221\257\353\303\234\336\270\317\212E\324\315\241X\202m\332\223b(\373\006\2534\324$\032?Z\n6\266y\373\rT\021\273\233\3019\3739\304\314\3749\227\242\t\234\256\206J\000v\214(UE\022#\361\222\001e\366\201Z/\004\304\327\033\223\241\034YU\236\316Q\262\364\357\206\310\362t\353\270\317:\021`\372\r\025\261\315]\336\233\000\317\3077/\306\306u\312\3320\243\363\232\253\002\213\355~a\215\3268Z\210.\261\241\254Y\332\316\rj\f\310X\217?\354H#\363\340\335\356\341M1\320DA\032<z\253\373\346\301\301\3415(2\276\313B\t<\211L\021P\272\233i\214\353bF\000tD)\223\301\300U\236w\237on\222\317\272\327`9x\262\230\346\n\2331\b\245m\006\203\303\200b\372\270\202\305\033\026t\352O\"`\240\243\241hC:\226\241S\a\363|\201\374\001+\272\326\234\3331\005\303\"\302\336\243 a\330\036\303\232\236\364@\024Tg\332Q\246\