  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining The Codebase**\n\nI\'m now implementing the first batch of edits. I\'ve streamlined `/src/pages/LandingPage.tsx`, removing redundant imports (`QRCodeSVG`, `Check`) and introducing `QrCode` and `KeyRound` from `lucide-react` for a cleaner look. I\'m focusing on ensuring everything is precisely aligned.\n\n\n**Updating The Hero**\n\nI\'ve just focused on the \"Mark your attendance\" hero card. I\'ve replaced the mock QR card with the intended clean design, complete with the localized titles and buttons: \"Scan QR\" and \"Enter ID\", leading to the respective `/mark` tabs. I\'m also ensuring the `/mark` route properly handles unauthenticated users, redirecting them to login and back. I\'m now reconsidering the hero\'s Login button, reviewing the requirements for redundancy.\n\n\n**Revising Authentication Flow**\n\nI\'m now implementing the redirect logic. I\'m using `useLocation()` in `ProtectedRoute.tsx` to handle unauthenticated users, redirecting them to `/login` with the current path as a state variable, as well as updating `LoginPage.tsx` to handle the return path when a user logs in. This ensures users are returned to their intended destinations after login. Admin users are properly handled in the process.\n\n\n**Implementing English Name Validation**\n\nI\'m now incorporating logic for English name validation across the registration and people management components. Specifically, I\'m integrating `needsEnglishNameForId` from `../utils/helpers` to determine when an English name input is necessary, and I\'ve implemented the required states and conditional rendering in `/src/pages/RegisterPage.tsx` and `/src/components/PeopleManagerView.tsx`. This includes validation and passing `englishName` to the relevant functions.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "VxH_ara7JIjQz7IPo5WO6AY"
