  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Critical Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the surgical upgrade plan, specifically the `/firestore.rules` file. I\'m verifying the server-side QR validation implementation. In `liveSecretValid(secret, data)`, the crucial requirement is `secret.active == true`, which confirms the QR code\'s active status. I\'m checking to ensure all security aspects are covered before any edits are made.\n\n\n**Enforcing Robust Security**\n\nI\'m now implementing stricter validation rules to enhance security. I\'ve added a critical `tokenUpdatedAt` timestamp requirement and a strict 10-second validity window server-side. I\'m rejecting any previous tokens, accepting ONLY the current active token. Plus, I\'m verifying the token and code string sizes for robustness. For attendance marking, I\'m ensuring explicit org matches, session status checks, end-time validity, and direct child session authorization.\n\n\n**Refining Session Permissions**\n\nI\'m now refining session permissions. I\'ve reevaluated the security protocols for `attendance` records, ensuring session secrets align with the correct organization and owner. I\'m focusing on `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` to make sure only the owner can read/write. I\'ve also strengthened the access controls within `sessions/{sessionId}`, and am implementing checks to verify the owner and organization match during record creation and updates.\n\n\n**Strengthening Token Integrity**\n\nI\'m now implementing crucial server-side token checks to prevent unauthorized access. I\'m ensuring that when `active` is `true`, the `tokenUpdatedAt` timestamp MUST match the server\'s time, making the token\'s validity time-sensitive. I\'ve updated `SessionSecret` to include `active` and `rotationSeq`, and will keep `prevToken`/`prevCode` optional for compatibility. I\'m focusing on atomic writes using `writeBatch` in `startAttendanceSession` and `rotateSessionSecret` with server timestamps and `increment(1)` for sequence tracking.\n\n\n**Finalizing Transactional Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating transactional logic to ensure data integrity. I\'ve added a `writeBatch` to update `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}`, guaranteeing the session is immediately marked as inactive. Moreover, I\'m introducing a real-time Firestore listener with `subscribeActiveParentSession` to allow lower-authority scanners to instantly view live sessions. To handle session mismatches, I\'m adding `resolveScannedSession` to classify scenarios such as unauthorized access, invalid QR codes, closed sessions, or valid sessions. I\'m also planning to use `runTransaction` to prevent duplicate attendance submissions.\n\n\n**Enhancing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing comprehensive error handling within the transaction. I\'m focusing on clearly distinguishing between network errors and various application-specific issues like expired tokens, duplicates, closed sessions, and device usage. I\'m building out a robust mechanism to categorize errors accurately, ensuring precise feedback to the user. I\'ve also integrated checks within the transactions to prevent data collisions and ensuring atomicity.\n\n\n\n**Optimizing Token Lifecycle**\n\nI\'m now refining the 10-second token rotation mechanism for reliability. I\'m focusing on using wall-clock time (`tokenIssuedAtMsRef`, `endsAtMsRef`) with `isRotatingRef` and `aborted` to ensure the `onSnapshot` updates do not reset the countdown. My goal is a consistent 10-second rotation with a visual countdown beneath the QR code, updating the display only after backend confirmation. I\'m also ensuring immediate token stop on session closure. The current features will be kept intact.\n\n\n**Improving Scanner Usability**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user experience enhancements for the QR scanner. I\'ll add a live session indicator card. I am adding a corner-bracket scanning frame with a `\"Verifying...\"` overlay. I\'m improving camera startup for both mobile and desktop setups, including appropriate fallback logic. To improve UX further, I\'ll add camera permission help and toast notifications. Finally, I\'m validating the scanned payloads against `resolveScannedSession` and `submitSelfAttendance` with specific error translations for a better UX.\n\n\n**Clarifying Error States**\n\nI\'m now diving into precise error state classifications. I am working on marking duplicate attendance attempts, along with scenarios of inactive or ended sessions. I am accounting for unauthorized access, incorrect organization or manager, and out-of-GPS area usage. I\'m handling the edge case of a device being used in the same session by someone else and, of course, the network being unavailable.\n\n\n**Defining Error Messages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on standardizing the user-facing error messages, creating a clear and consistent set of translations. I\'ve compiled several error messages, including the Hindi translations, to maintain 100% key parity across `en.json` and `hi.json` files, and I\'ll test these. I am also working on `README.md` to document the strict server-side 10-second QR expiration and the atomic Firestore operations.\n\n\n"
