    }
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_12687791128967437638"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Update README with strict 10-second server-side QR validation and atomic Firestore transaction details\", \"EndLine\":28, \"Instruction\":\"Update Live Rotating QR Sessions and Zero-Cloud-Functions Security bullets in README.md.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  - **Projector Mode**: Full-screen view with Screen Wake Lock API, visible **LIVE** status indicator, large QR rotating every **10 seconds** (`{ \\\"s\\\": sessionId, \\\"t\\\": token }` with 128-bit crypto tokens) with a circular countdown ring and 10s timer, synchronized **6-digit live code**, live `\\\"Marked: X / Y\\\"` counter, real-time marked feed, real-time `\\\"Rejected attempts\\\"` list, `\\\"Extend 10 min\\\"`, and `\\\"Stop session\\\"` (immediately invalidates the active token).\\n- **Self-Marking & QR Scanner (`/mark`)**:\\n  - Real-time subscription to the direct parent\'s active LIVE session (Manager scans Admin\'s session; Member scans their Manager\'s session).\\n  - Automatic GPS verification (`\\\"You are 12 m from the class \342\234\223\\\"` / `\\\"You are 340 m away \342\234\227\\\"`), rejecting readings with accuracy > 100 m.\\n  - Dedicated camera **QR Scanner** with scanning frame overlay (mobile back/front camera + desktop webcam fallback) and **Enter ID** (6-char own ID + 6-digit live code) tab.\\n  - Uses a **Firestore Transaction (`runTransaction`)** to atomically check session status, prevent duplicate attendance per user, and record attendance with zero race conditions.\\n- **Server-Side Security (`firestore.rules` \342\200\224 No Cloud Functions Required)**:\\n  - Rotating secrets stored in `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` (strictly readable/writable only by the session starter, verified server-side by Firestore Security Rules).\\n  - **Strict 10-second backend TTL**: Only the currently active token/code is accepted (`request.time <= secret.tokenUpdatedAt + duration.value(10, \'s\')` and `secret.active == true`). Previous tokens and ended sessions are immediately rejected by Firestore on the server.\\n  - Server-side role & organization checks (`orgId`, direct parent-child hierarchy), flat-earth radius check (`cosLat`, `math.sqrt`, `math.pow`), atomic one-device-per-session lock (`sessionDevices/{sessionId}_{deviceId}`), and `attempts/{id}` logging.\", \"StartLine\":14, \"TargetContent\":\"  - **Projector Mode**: Full-screen view with Screen Wake Lock API, large QR rotating every **10 seconds** (`{ \\\"s\\\": sessionId, \\\"t\\\": token }`) with a countdown ring, synchronized **6-digit live code**, live `\\\"Marked: X / Y\\\"` counter, real-time marked feed, real-time `\\\"Rejected attempts\\\"` list, `\\\"Extend 10 min\\\"`, and `\\\"Close session\\\"`.\\n- **Self-Marking Page (`/mark`)**:\\n  - Automatic GPS verification (`\\\"You are 12 m from the class \342\234\223\\\"` / `\\\"You are 340 m away \342\234\227\\\"`), rejecting readings with accuracy > 100 m.\\n  - Two tabs: **Scan QR** (live rotating QR camera scanner) and **Enter ID** (6-char own ID + 6-digit live code).\\n  - Automatically marks **Late** after the organization\'s `lateAfter` cut-off time.\\n- **Zero-Cloud-Functions Security (`firestore.rules`)**:\\n  - Rotating secrets stored in `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` (readable/writable only by the session starter, verified server-side by Firestore Security Rules).\\n  - Current token/code valid max 15 seconds; previous token/code valid 5 seconds after rotation for network delay.\\n  - Server-side flat-earth radius check (`cosLat`, `math.sqrt`, `math.pow`) enforced in `firestore.rules`.\\n  - Atomic one-device-per-session lock via `sessionDevices/{sessionId}_{deviceId}` written in the same `writeBatch` as the attendance record.\\n  - Failed attempts logged to `attempts/{id}` and shown live on the session screen.\", \"TargetFile\":\"/README.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating README security and transaction notes\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update README.md\"}"
      original_name: "replace_file_content"
    }
