  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nThe user requested implementing and hardening a complete **Dynamic QR-Based Live Attendance System** directly inside their existing **Smart Attendance System** (`attendence-92251` Firebase project, React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind v4) without breaking or removing any existing functionality (roles, hierarchy `Admin \342\206\222 Managers \342\206\222 Members`, dashboards, reports, leaves, notices, English/Hindi i18n, dark mode, Leaflet GPS map, 6-char unique IDs, backup manual mode, PWA).\n\n### Core Requirements & Success Criteria\n1. **Higher Authority \342\200\223 Dynamic QR Generator (`/attendance`, `StartAttendancePage.tsx`)**:\n   - Start Live Attendance Session, display large QR code rotating automatically every **10 seconds** with a visible 10-second countdown timer and secure unique 128-bit token per rotation.\n   - Show clear **LIVE** status indicator + session details + **Stop session** button that immediately stops token generation and invalidates the active token.\n2. **Lower Authority \342\200\223 QR Scanner (`/mark`, `MarkYourAttendancePage.tsx` + `ManagerDashboard.tsx` / `MemberDashboard.tsx`)**:\n   - Dedicated QR Scanner option in Manager/Teacher and Member dashboards.\n   - Camera scanning on both mobile and desktop (with automatic webcam fallback), scanning frame overlay, permission handling, automatic QR detection/validation, immediate attendance marking, success notification, and clear error messages for expired, invalid, already-used, unauthorized, network-error, or ended-session QR codes.\n3. **Strict 10-Second Server-Side Validation (`firestore.rules`)**:\n   - Each QR code valid for **strictly 10 seconds** on Firestore\'s server clock (`request.time <= secret.tokenUpdatedAt + duration.value(10, \'s\')`).\n   - Previous QR tokens are immediately invalidated upon rotation (no grace period / no `prevToken` accepted) and when the session stops (`secret.active == false`).\n   - Cannot be bypassed by frontend JS timers, fake/tampered QR payloads, or unauthorized users; `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` is strictly owner-only.\n4. **Atomic Attendance Recording (`sessionService.ts`)**:\n   - Records `personUid`, `sessionId`, `orgId`, `timestamp` (`serverTimestamp()`), `status` (`present`/`late`), etc. in the existing `attendance` collection (`{orgId}_{date}_{personUid}`) with zero unnecessary duplicate collections.\n   - Uses a **Firestore Transaction (`runTransaction`)** + backend rules (`!exists`, `existsAfter(sessionDevices)`) to prevent race conditions and duplicate attendance per user per session while allowing multiple distinct users on their own devices to scan the same active QR.\n5. **Final Reporting**: Report all modified files and the exact Firebase deployment steps (`firestore.rules` + `firestore.indexes.json`) the user needs to perform on `attendence-92251`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n\n### Completed Edits (Not Yet Compiled/Linted After Latest Batch)\nAll code and configuration changes for the Dynamic QR-Based Live Attendance System are **complete**:\n- **`/firestore.rules`**:\n  - Tightened `liveSecretValid(secret, data)` to enforce `secret.active == true`, `secret.tokenUpdatedAt is timestamp`, `request.time >= secret.tokenUpdatedAt && request.time <= secret.tokenUpdatedAt + duration.value(10, \'s\')`, and removed `prevToken`/`prevCode` acceptance so ONLY the currently active 128-bit `token` (size >= 32) or 6-digit `code` (size == 6) is accepted.\n  - Hardened `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` create/update rules to enforce `request.resource.data.tokenUpdatedAt == request.time` (server-authoritative timestamp) and strict `ownerUid == request.auth.uid`.\n  - Hardened `canSelfMarkAttendance(recordId)` with explicit `!exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/attendance/$(recordId))`, `sess.orgId == request.resource.data.orgId`, `secret.orgId == sess.orgId`, and `secret.ownerUid == sess.ownerUid`.\n  - Previously hardened `allow get` on `sessionDevices` and `attendance` against `resource == null`, and guarded `canSelfMarkAttendance` behind `method in [\'live_qr\', \'live_code\']` so manual backup writes never fail on missing `sessionId`.\n- **`/src/types/index.ts`**:\n  - Updated `SessionSecret` interface with `active: boolean` and optional `rotationSeq?: number`, `prevToken?`, `prevCode?`.\n- **`/src/services/sessionService.ts`**:\n  - `startAttendanceSession`: Atomically creates `sessions/{sessionId}` and `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` (`active: true`, `rotationSeq: 1`, `tokenUpdatedAt: serverTimestamp()`) in one `writeBatch`.\n  - `rotateSessionSecret`: Overwrites `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` with a fresh 128-bit `crypto.getRandomValues` token + 6-digit code (`prevToken: \'\'`, `prevCode: \'\'`, `rotationSeq: increment(1)`, `tokenUpdatedAt: serverTimestamp()`), immediately invalidating the old token on the backend.\n  - `closeAttendanceSession`: Atomically closes `sessions/{sessionId}` (`status: \'closed\'`, `closedAt: serverTimestamp()`) AND invalidates `sessionSecrets/{sessionId}` (`active: false`, `token: \'\'`, `code: \'\'`) in one `writeBatch`.\n  - Added `getDirectParentUid`, `isAuthorizedForSession`, real-time `subscribeActiveParentSession`, and `resolveScannedSession` (resolves any scanned `sessionId` directly against Firestore to distinguish `closed`, `unauthorized`, `not_found`, and `network` errors).\n  - Upgraded `submitSelfAttendance` to use **`runTransaction`** (reads `sessions`, `attendance`, `sessionDevices`, then writes `sessionDevices` and `attendance` atomically) with clean classification of `errExpired`, `errInvalidCode`, `errSessionClosed`, `errAlreadyMarked`, `errDeviceUsed`, `errUnauthorized`, `errOutsideArea`, and `errNetwork`.\n- **`/src/pages/StartAttendancePage.tsx`**:\n  - Added visible **LIVE** status indicator (pulsing dot + `LIVE` label) and session details (short Session ID, target role, remaining session duration, allowed radius, wake lock).\n  - Fixed the 10-second rotation timer to use wall-clock elapsed time (`tokenIssuedAtMsRef`) + `endsAtMsRef` + `isRotatingRef` + `aborted` flag so Firestore `onSnapshot` updates never reset the rotation timer mid-cycle, rotates cleanly every ~9.6s (staying strictly inside the 10s backend TTL), updates the displayed QR only after Firestore commits the new token, and immediately stops generation and clears `currentToken`/`currentCode` when **Stop session** is clicked or duration ends.\n  - Upgraded the 10-second countdown display with a prominent numeric countdown (`10s` \342\206\222 `1s`) alongside the SVG countdown ring and `\"Refreshing QR...\"` status.\n- **`/src/pages/MarkYourAttendancePage.tsx`**:\n  - Switched from one-shot fetch to real-time `subscribeActiveParentSession` so LIVE sessions appear and end automatically without reload (plus local `endsAt` auto-expiry timer).\n  - Kept the QR Scanner accessible even when no active session banner is shown, validating any scanned QR\'s `sessionId` via `resolveScannedSession` so scanning an ended/unauthorized/wrong-org QR immediately returns an accurate error.\n  - Added a clean corner-bracket scanning frame overlay with `\"Verifying...\"` / `\"Align the live QR code inside the frame\"` guidance.\n  - Added desktop webcam fallback (`Html5Qrcode.getCameras()`) when `{ facingMode }` fails on desktop browsers.\n  - Added Toast notifications alongside inline success/error cards.\n- **`/src/pages/ManagerDashboard.tsx`**:\n  - Updated the Manager\'s `/mark` CTA to link directly to `/mark?tab=scan` labeled `\"QR Scanner\"` (`t(\'mark.qrScannerBtn\')`) alongside `\"Start attendance\"` (`/attendance`).\n- **`/src/i18n/en.json` & `/src/i18n/hi.json`**:\n  - Added matching English & Hindi strings (`session.liveBadge`, `session.sessionIdLabel`, `session.rotatingToken`, `session.closeBtn` \342\206\222 `\"Stop session\"`, `mark.qrScannerBtn`, `mark.liveSessionActive`, `mark.scanFrameHint`, `mark.errUnauthorized`, `mark.errNetwork`, and updated `mark.errExpired` / `mark.errSessionClosed` / `mark.errAlreadyMarked`).\n- **`/README.md`**:\n  - Updated documentation for strict 10-second server-side QR TTL, real-time scanner sync, and Firestore transactions.\n\n### Not Yet Done\n- **Final Verification** has NOT been run yet since the latest edits above:\n  1. Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in parallel, plus verify `en.json`/`hi.json` key parity.\n  2. Fix any compilation, TypeScript, or i18n issues if found.\n  3. Present a clear final summary listing all modified files, how the 10 test scenarios are satisfied, and exact Firebase deployment steps for `attendence-92251`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Zero-Cloud-Functions Backend Validation**: The user\'s Firebase project (`attendence-92251`) is configured for the free Spark plan (no Cloud Functions required). All critical security checks run **server-side in `firestore.rules`** using `request.time`, `request.auth`, `get(sessionSecrets)`, `existsAfter(sessionDevices)`, and `runTransaction`, so frontend JS timer tampering or payload forgery cannot bypass the 10-second expiry or role/org checks.\n- **Previous `StartAttendancePage` Timer Bug Fixed**: Previously, `useEffect` depended on `activeSession?.endsAt` (a new `Timestamp` reference on every Firestore snapshot), which could reset the 10s interval mid-cycle. Fixed by tracking `endsAtMsRef` and wall-clock `tokenIssuedAtMsRef` with `activeSession?.id` as the sole dependency.\n- **Desktop Camera Fallback**: Desktop webcams often throw `OverconstrainedError` on `{ facingMode: \'environment\' }`. `MarkYourAttendancePage` now falls back automatically to `Html5Qrcode.getCameras()`.\n- **Pre-existing Codebase Build Health**: Before this turn\'s edits, `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) both passed cleanly, and `en.json`/`hi.json` had exact 481-key parity (now ~489 keys after adding the new keys).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- No build or lint errors have occurred yet in this turn (verification has not been run after the latest edits).\n- **Bug Fixed Proactively**:\n  - `StartAttendancePage.tsx` previously passed `{ sessionId, prevToken, prevCode }` to `rotateSessionSecret`; updated call sites to `{ sessionId }`. Verify via `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) that no stale references to `prevToken` or old signatures remain anywhere.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- All file edits for the Dynamic QR-Based Live Attendance System are saved on disk.\n- No background tasks, dev server restarts, or external provisioning steps are pending.\n- Firebase project ID: `attendence-92251` (`src/firebase.ts` untouched, using exact existing config).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Run Final Verification in Parallel**:\n   - Call `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, and a quick `run_command` node one-liner checking `en.json` vs `hi.json` key parity (zero missing keys in either file).\n2. **Fix Any Errors**:\n   - If `compile_applet` or `lint_applet` reports any error (e.g., unused import or type mismatch), fix it and re-run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together.\n3. **Final User Report**:\n   - Summarize the completed implementation cleanly, explicitly listing:\n     - All files modified (`firestore.rules`, `src/types/index.ts`, `src/services/sessionService.ts`, `src/pages/StartAttendancePage.tsx`, `src/pages/MarkYourAttendancePage.tsx`, `src/pages/ManagerDashboard.tsx`, `src/i18n/en.json`, `src/i18n/hi.json`, `README.md`).\n     - How all 10 verification scenarios work end-to-end.\n     - Exact Firebase deployment steps the user must run/perform in Firebase Console or CLI for `attendence-92251`:\n       1. Publish updated `firestore.rules` (`firebase deploy --only firestore:rules` or paste into Firebase Console \342\206\222 Firestore Database \342\206\222 Rules \342\206\222 Publish).\n       2. Deploy/verify composite indexes from `firestore.indexes.json` (`firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes`), especially `sessions (orgId, ownerUid, status)`, `attendance (orgId, sessionId)`, and `attempts (orgId, sessionId, time)`.\n       3. Ensure HTTPS / authorized domains are enabled for camera & GPS access.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do NOT break or remove any existing features (roles, hierarchy, dashboards, reports, leaves, notices, Hindi/English toggle, dark mode, 6-char IDs, backup manual mode, Leaflet GPS map, PWA).\n- Do NOT alter `src/firebase.ts` credentials or expose any admin/secret keys in frontend code.\n- Do NOT add duplicate attendance collections; stay compatible with existing `attendance`, `sessions`, `sessionSecrets`, `sessionDevices`, `attempts` collections.\n- Keep responses concise, scannable, and free of internal tool/step details.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 107
