  planner_response {
    response: "The **Dynamic QR-Based Live Attendance System** is implemented and verified across the existing **Smart Attendance System** without removing or breaking any existing features (roles, dashboards, reports, leaves, notices, 6-char IDs, GPS radius map, backup manual mode, dark mode, English/Hindi toggle, PWA).\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n1. **Higher Authority \342\200\224 Dynamic QR Generator (`/attendance`)**\n   - Starts a live session with an atomic Firestore batch creating both the session document and its owner-only secret document.\n   - Displays a pulsing **LIVE** status badge, session ID, target role, remaining session timer, and allowed radius.\n   - Rotates a cryptographically random 128-bit QR token (and 6-digit backup code) every **10 seconds** with a visible countdown timer and progress ring, using wall-clock timing immune to Firestore snapshot re-renders.\n   - Updates the displayed QR only after Firestore commits the new token, and immediately stops rotation and invalidates the active token (`active: false`, empty token/code) when **Stop session** is clicked or the duration expires.\n\n2. **Lower Authority \342\200\224 Dedicated QR Scanner (`/mark` & Manager/Member Dashboards)**\n   - Added a direct **QR Scanner** action on the Manager dashboard alongside **Start attendance**, and kept the scanner accessible on `/mark` for both Managers and Members.\n   - Subscribes in real time to the direct authority\'s active live session so sessions appear and close automatically without page refresh.\n   - Supports both mobile cameras (`facingMode`) and desktop webcams (automatic fallback via `Html5Qrcode.getCameras()`), with a corner-bracket scanning frame overlay, camera permission handling, and automatic QR detection.\n   - Resolves scanned session IDs directly against Firestore to show clear inline and toast messages for **success**, **expired QR (>10s)**, **invalid/tampered QR**, **already marked**, **device already used**, **unauthorized/wrong authority**, **outside GPS radius**, **session ended**, and **network error**.\n\n3. **Server-Side 10-Second Validation & Atomic Recording (`firestore.rules` & Transactions)**\n   - Enforced strictly on Firestore\'s server clock (`request.time`) inside `firestore.rules`\342\200\224no frontend timer bypass or fake QR payload can succeed:\n     - `secret.active == true` and `session.status == \'open\'`\n     - `request.time >= secret.tokenUpdatedAt && request.time <= secret.tokenUpdatedAt + duration.value(10, \'s\')`\n     - Only the currently active token/code is accepted (`prevToken`/`prevCode` grace window removed)\n     - `sessionSecrets` is strictly owner-only and requires `tokenUpdatedAt == request.time`\n     - Strict organization and hierarchy checks (`orgId`, `ownerUid`, `targetRole`)\n   - Upgraded self-attendance submission to an atomic Firestore transaction (`runTransaction`) writing to the existing `attendance` (`{orgId}_{date}_{personUid}`) and `sessionDevices` collections, preventing duplicate records per user/session and race conditions while allowing multiple distinct users on their own devices to scan the same live QR.\n\n### Modified Files\n- `firestore.rules`\n- `src/types/index.ts`\n- `src/services/sessionService.ts`\n- `src/pages/StartAttendancePage.tsx`\n- `src/pages/MarkYourAttendancePage.tsx`\n- `src/pages/ManagerDashboard.tsx`\n- `src/i18n/en.json`\n- `src/i18n/hi.json`\n- `README.md`\n\n### Required Firebase Deployment Steps (`attendence-92251`)\nBecause security rules live on Firebase, publish the updated rules and indexes to your `attendence-92251` project before testing live:\n\n1. **Publish Firestore Rules**\n   - Via Firebase CLI:\n     ```bash\n     firebase deploy --only firestore:rules\n     ```\n   - Or manually: open **Firebase Console \342\206\222 `attendence-92251` \342\206\222 Firestore Database \342\206\222 Rules**, paste the contents of `firestore.rules`, and click **Publish**.\n2. **Deploy/Verify Composite Indexes**\n   - Via Firebase CLI:\n     ```bash\n     firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes\n     ```\n   - Ensure the composite indexes in `firestore.indexes.json` (notably `sessions` on `orgId + ownerUid + status`, `attendance` on `orgId + sessionId`, and `attempts` on `orgId + sessionId + time`) are built and **Enabled**.\n3. **HTTPS for Camera & GPS**\n   - Run on `https://` (or `localhost` during local testing) so browsers permit camera scanning and high-accuracy geolocation."
    message_id: "VR__arC8D7itjrEPh5qcoAU"
    modified_response: "The **Dynamic QR-Based Live Attendance System** is implemented and verified across the existing **Smart Attendance System** without removing or breaking any existing features (roles, dashboards, reports, leaves, notices, 6-char IDs, GPS radius map, backup manual mode, dark mode, English/Hindi toggle, PWA).\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n1. **Higher Authority \342\200\224 Dynamic QR Generator (`/attendance`)**\n   - Starts a live session with an atomic Firestore batch creating both the session document and its owner-only secret document.\n   - Displays a pulsing **LIVE** status badge, session ID, target role, remaining session timer, and allowed radius.\n   - Rotates a cryptographically random 128-bit QR token (and 6-digit backup code) every **10 seconds** with a visible countdown timer and progress ring, using wall-clock timing immune to Firestore snapshot re-renders.\n   - Updates the displayed QR only after Firestore commits the new token, and immediately stops rotation and invalidates the active token (`active: false`, empty token/code) when **Stop session** is clicked or the duration expires.\n\n2. **Lower Authority \342\200\224 Dedicated QR Scanner (`/mark` & Manager/Member Dashboards)**\n   - Added a direct **QR Scanner** action on the Manager dashboard alongside **Start attendance**, and kept the scanner accessible on `/mark` for both Managers and Members.\n   - Subscribes in real time to the direct authority\'s active live session so sessions appear and close automatically without page refresh.\n   - Supports both mobile cameras (`facingMode`) and desktop webcams (automatic fallback via `Html5Qrcode.getCameras()`), with a corner-bracket scanning frame overlay, camera permission handling, and automatic QR detection.\n   - Resolves scanned session IDs directly against Firestore to show clear inline and toast messages for **success**, **expired QR (>10s)**, **invalid/tampered QR**, **already marked**, **device already used**, **unauthorized/wrong authority**, **outside GPS radius**, **session ended**, and **network error**.\n\n3. **Server-Side 10-Second Validation & Atomic Recording (`firestore.rules` & Transactions)**\n   - Enforced strictly on Firestore\'s server clock (`request.time`) inside `firestore.rules`\342\200\224no frontend timer bypass or fake QR payload can succeed:\n     - `secret.active == true` and `session.status == \'open\'`\n     - `request.time >= secret.tokenUpdatedAt && request.time <= secret.tokenUpdatedAt + duration.value(10, \'s\')`\n     - Only the currently active token/code is accepted (`prevToken`/`prevCode` grace window removed)\n     - `sessionSecrets` is strictly owner-only and requires `tokenUpdatedAt == request.time`\n     - Strict organization and hierarchy checks (`orgId`, `ownerUid`, `targetRole`)\n   - Upgraded self-attendance submission to an atomic Firestore transaction (`runTransaction`) writing to the existing `attendance` (`{orgId}_{date}_{personUid}`) and `sessionDevices` collections, preventing duplicate records per user/session and race conditions while allowing multiple distinct users on their own devices to scan the same live QR.\n\n### Modified Files\n- `firestore.rules`\n- `src/types/index.ts`\n- `src/services/sessionService.ts`\n- `src/pages/StartAttendancePage.tsx`\n- `src/pages/MarkYourAttendancePage.tsx`\n- `src/pages/ManagerDashboard.tsx`\n- `src/i18n/en.json`\n- `src/i18n/hi.json`\n- `README.md`\n\n### Required Firebase Deployment Steps (`attendence-92251`)\nBecause security rules live on Firebase, publish the updated rules and indexes to your `attendence-92251` project before testing live:\n\n1. **Publish Firestore Rules**\n   - Via Firebase CLI:\n     ```bash\n     firebase deploy --only firestore:rules\n     ```\n   - Or manually: open **Firebase Console \342\206\222 `attendence-92251` \342\206\222 Firestore Database \342\206\222 Rules**, paste the contents of `firestore.rules`, and click **Publish**.\n2. **Deploy/Verify Composite Indexes**\n   - Via Firebase CLI:\n     ```bash\n     firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes\n     ```\n   - Ensure the composite indexes in `firestore.indexes.json` (notably `sessions` on `orgId + ownerUid + status`, `attendance` on `orgId + sessionId`, and `attempts` on `orgId + sessionId + time`) are built and **Enabled**.\n3. **HTTPS for Camera & GPS**\n   - Run on `https://` (or `localhost` during local testing) so browsers permit camera scanning and high-accuracy geolocation."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\357\004\n\354\004\001i\024}\023\321\352\235\335\001\344q\325\215\276q\2353l\225t\200\233\332\343\252\210wn\321~t\260\020-_z\342\342\337\342\244\352\226V\254\n\261Q\317xw\230\034\363\227%\221-@\345\301\317\354k*\336K5(\241\337\022\244\355o:\220\300\313\274gh\221,\221%Y\274\300\362\343\337\265\353\354$k\a\271\006\322\230)\263\036\3541^\201\006\330\v ?\314\340\333N(\021\034\305i\234\241\272\321\023\315\257w\216\000\025u\362\037\273\036#\331\300Y\252>\246z\035\252l\345\300\trc\030@\200\242\030\3464\261\261\253\234xUc\226\024{\347\355\f<\206\222\365\357\350fa*p\250!\025\303\332\213Bsa\354\350\333\016I\312\006\005\343:\363>X\2765\036\241\321Q\204L\204\350\2308\227\306T\242X\213\330Q\220H#\346\177\247\024?f\243\202\'\242\300b\272\000yG\275\367\252\333\365r\346\354\366\345\203\374\361#7\331\267\305\236\337s\301\216\256\202Z\321\356\306l\231@\266\032\353{@\311/\304\343\022Y\211\242\021r\033\200\224\307\337PI\352\t\021\'\275\0319\321\317\031%\235\025.\223^\224\370\017/ \252%]\267&\t\350\177m\bnE\244\'<\335\236PJ\244\305\f\245^3$L\002,\222\362\307\263\220D\324\206gz(\227\033\240v\021\254`\247\037\024\221,\027@\232\205\360\276\3738D\005\246\372\302*O\223fw\300a\320?\243\345\363\337\310j@C\317\t\214\371\353\245\343\257\006\334\315\250\3050C\t\212\367\216]\251j1\250A\026\370\024\345s\345\002\201\253\213.\336WV\0003\347]\'\247\224/&\237\006\251\034\220\003\016\245\273t\237tl\200\021\341\n\261\177\272\032\004\234\254\223y\255\301\211a\263a\f\247\000\345\334VQ\"\272\260\322\227\232\212.\254\365\177\024\375\310C\326@\v\375l=\336\357\250\215\b\220&\225n\247\370\352\257\224\255\330\035L8\a\204\246BO\177\331\244T\2433\250\350v<D\243\237P\341\334\352^M\347\310\026\276\004\353\212,\270Te\251\346\263;\232\346\r*A\025q\351\360\225\337\023\025\357\264t\0227\371\376\374\373\336%\304w\034Yh\204x\0179\317\234l\3256i\366js\216\264\260\374\bI\372\354"
