  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Core Services**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the core services. Specifically, I\'m building out `auditService.ts`, which will handle immutable audit logging, and `academicService.ts`, which I\'m designing with full CRUD operations and flexible querying capabilities. I\'m prioritizing strong data integrity and efficient access.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the data scope. I\'m focusing on new services for departments, classes, subjects, faculty assignments, and timetables with conflict detection. Also, I\'m working on parent links for profile management and linking, as well as a Super Admin organization directory.\n\n\n**Defining Session Access**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining session access. I\'m implementing mechanisms to prevent duplicate open sessions for teachers and subjects or timetable slots. Audit logging for session starts is a priority. I\'m also building a real-time listener, `subscribeEligibleLiveSessions`, that handles concurrent teacher and subject sessions for students, managers, and admins, with explicit error handling for permission, network, and index issues. I\'m also creating `findEligibleLiveSessions` to back \"Check again\".\n\n\n**Tracking Session Presence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on real-time active sessions. I\'m building `RecentSessionsByOwner` to allow for clean session management. Also, I\'m developing `submitSelfAttendance`, which strictly sets attendance to \"present\" with deterministic, session-scoped doc IDs. Further, it prevents overwrites and ensures audit logging. Finally, I\'ve updated `attendanceService.ts` to eliminate \"late\" statuses completely.\n\n\n**Refining Attendance Data**\n\nI\'m now refining attendance data. I\'ve added functions to fetch attendance by class and teacher, addressing both teacher UID and manager ID scenarios. Real-time updates for student dashboards are enabled through `subscribeAttendanceForPerson`, and audit logs now track every attendance action. I have also removed \"late\" statuses entirely, ensuring data consistency.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "gDD_atL1HdHQz7IP49ShoQ4"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4466862426846864844"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import {\\n  addDoc,\\n  collection,\\n  getDocs,\\n  limit,\\n  orderBy,\\n  query,\\n  serverTimestamp,\\n  where,\\n} from \'firebase/firestore\';\\nimport { db } from \'../firebase\';\\nimport type { AuditLog, UserProfile } from \'../types\';\\n\\nexport async function recordAuditLog(params: {\\n  actor: Pick<UserProfile, \'uid\' | \'name\' | \'role\' | \'orgId\'>;\\n  action: AuditLog[\'action\'];\\n  targetCollection: string;\\n  targetId: string;\\n  summary: string;\\n  metadata?: Record<string, string | number | boolean | null>;\\n}): Promise<void> {\\n  if (!params.actor?.uid || !params.actor?.orgId) return;\\n  try {\\n    await addDoc(collection(db, \'auditLogs\'), {\\n      orgId: params.actor.orgId,\\n      actorUid: params.actor.uid,\\n      actorName: params.actor.name || \'User\',\\n      actorRole: params.actor.role,\\n      action: params.action,\\n      targetCollection: params.targetCollection,\\n      targetId: params.targetId,\\n      summary: params.summary,\\n      metadata: params.metadata || {},\\n      timestamp: serverTimestamp(),\\n    });\\n  } catch {\\n    // Non-blocking: audit log failure must not crash user flow if offline/rules not yet deployed\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function fetchAuditLogs(\\n  orgId: string,\\n  maxItems = 150\\n): Promise<AuditLog[]> {\\n  try {\\n    const q = query(\\n      collection(db, \'auditLogs\'),\\n      where(\'orgId\', \'==\', orgId),\\n      orderBy(\'timestamp\', \'desc\'),\\n      limit(maxItems)\\n    );\\n    const snap = await getDocs(q);\\n    return snap.docs.map((d) => ({ ...(d.data() as Omit<AuditLog, \'id\'>), id: d.id }));\\n  } catch {\\n    // Fallback without orderBy in case composite index is still building\\n    const q = query(collection(db, \'auditLogs\'), where(\'orgId\', \'==\', orgId));\\n    const snap = await getDocs(q);\\n    return snap.docs\\n      .map((d) => ({ ...(d.data() as Omit<AuditLog, \'id\'>), id: d.id }))\\n      .sort((a, b) => (b.timestamp?.toMillis?.() ?? 0) - (a.timestamp?.toMillis?.() ?? 0))\\n      .slice(0, maxItems);\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create immutable audit logging service writing to append-only auditLogs collection\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/services/auditService.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating auditService.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create auditService.ts\"}"
